:0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in v4.7.beta5.official [bbd3f43b5] and v4.7.dev1.official [bf95b6258] (first official build with the trackball feature)\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.7.beta5 - Windows 11 (build 26200) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Direct3D 12 (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3070 Ti Laptop GPU (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.7260) - AMD Ryzen 7 6800H with Radeon Graphics (16 threads) - 23.26 GiB memory - WASAPI (48000 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\nTrackball rotation doesn't behave as expected when `Use Local Space` is toggled in the toolbar. \nIt should behave exactly the same when the transform is in local space or world space, because trackball rotation is a **screen space transformation**.\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0f06ff86-8cfd-43f5-856c-e8146bf80073\n\nThe bug is present since the first official build with the new trackball feature (4.7.dev1.official), so I suggest it comes from the inital implementation #109976\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Create a Node3D, for example a `MeshInstance3D` with a simple BoxMesh\n2. Set its rotation to anything other than neutral, for example `90,0,0`\n3. Toggle `Use Local Space` and `Use Trackball` in the viewport toolbar\n4. Rotate with the trackball feature. The resulting rotation is not correct\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owne